WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.500
Step 1: As an OpStack owner, open Console → Billing. Start in Sandbox, enter the Stripe test secret key and save. Keep Live and Sandbox credentials separate; blank secret fields preserve the saved values.

2
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:22.375
Step 2: Set APP_ORIGIN to the public HTTPS app address. Create the displayed webhook endpoint in Stripe with API version 2024-06-20, for checkout.session.completed, customer.subscription.*, invoice.* and charge.refunded. Save its matching signing secret.

3
00:00:22.375 --> 00:00:32.333
Step 3: Choose Test connection &amp; sync. Check Connected and the last report sync. Imports read every page before replacing the previous results; failures retain the last completed report.

4
00:00:32.333 --> 00:00:46.333
Step 4: Create two recurring AUD monthly per-unit prices in Stripe. In OpStack Billing, add a location and choose Create Stripe customer. Enter the paying business/legal name, billing email and address, then choose Review customer. Your other location-plan entries stay as drafts.

5
00:00:46.333 --> 00:01:02.208
Step 5: Check the reviewed business details, then choose Create customer in Stripe. Matching full details offer Use existing customer instead. The customer ID fills automatically; other locations can use Use saved customer. Enter the price IDs and save billing settings. Creating a customer does not start billing.

6
00:01:02.208 --> 00:01:19.958
Step 6: Review billing and check the rates, user count and tax treatment. For a new subscription, create the hosted checkout link and let the customer finish it. Sync, then review and apply quantities. For automatic updates, select the plan checkbox, save and review/apply, then enable automatic sync. Changes prorate on the next invoice.

7
00:01:19.958 --> 00:01:34.292
Step 7: Open Monthly report → Collections for linked paid invoices, open amounts, refunds and uncollectible invoices. Choose Sandbox explicitly for test results. Manage taxes, receipts, refunds and cancellations in Stripe. Stop old GoCardless subscriptions there before starting Stripe to avoid double billing.
